# Practical 4 – Implementation and Time Analysis of Factorial Program

## Aim
To implement and analyze the factorial program using **Iterative and Recursive methods**.

## Description
Factorial of a number `n` is the product of all positive integers from `1` to `n`.

Example:
`5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 120`

### Iterative Method
Uses a `for` loop to calculate the factorial.

### Recursive Method
The function calls itself until it reaches the base case `0` or `1`.

## Sample Input
```text
Enter a number: 5
````

## Output

```text
Factorial using Iterative Method: 120
Time Complexity: O(n)
Execution Time: 0.000002 seconds

Factorial using Recursive Method: 120
Time Complexity: O(n)
Execution Time: 0.000002 seconds
```

## Complexity

| Method    | Time Complexity | Space Complexity |
| --------- | --------------- | ---------------- |
| Iterative | O(n)            | O(1)             |
| Recursive | O(n)            | O(n)             |

## Conclusion

Both iterative and recursive methods successfully calculate the factorial. Both have **O(n)** time complexity, but the iterative method uses less memory.

